Reused verbatim or near-verbatim:

- `PROTOCOL.md` — protocol documentation (copied, with a status note added at the top)
- `udev/70-ak820.rules` — device permission rule
- the entire web UI under `apps/desktop/ui/` (HTML, CSS, `app.js`, `gen.js`, `fx.js`,
  and `ak820.js` up to its transport layer), including all generators and effects

Reimplemented in Rust by this project:

- HID transport (discovery, report sizing, chunking, retries, locking)
- animation payload packing/unpacking (validated against the upstream JavaScript byte-for-byte)
- history storage (SQLite instead of IndexedDB)
- clock autosync service, tray, autostart, packaging

`ak820.py` from upstream was used as a behavioural reference for the transport and CLI; it is not
vendored here.

